gate command (JVM; paste it, do not retype the module names):
  sbt -batch "acquireJVM/test; alignJVM/test; amrInteropJVM/test; codecJVM/test; coreJVM/test; corpusJVM/test; corpusIntake/test; documentJVM/test; embedBench/test; embedCoreJVM/test; embedGrakern/test; fixturesJVM/test; interviewJVM/test; lawsJVM/test; media/test; pipeline/test; propositionJVM/test; providerAgent/test; storyJVM/test; viewJVM/test"

  Run it in a CLONE, never a linked worktree. Capture the exit status. Run
  scalafmtCheckAll LAST, separately. Then grep the log for 'Passed: Total' --
  a red gate with no totals measured your infrastructure, not the candidate.
